  "nl_text": "The rschema_0110 database is designed to manage user interactions and content updates within a social media platform. The User table stores information about each user, including their avatar path, creation and last modification times, date of birth, email address, phone number, and unique username, which serves as the primary key. The Update table contains updates posted by users, with each update having a unique ID, content, content type, posting time, and a foreign key referencing the User table to identify the user who made the update. The Follow_Relationship table tracks friendships between users, with each relationship having a follow time and referencing the IDs of both the follower and the user being followed, with both IDs serving as foreign keys referencing the User table. The Comment table stores comments made on updates, with each comment having a unique ID, content, comment time, and referencing the ID of the user who made the comment and the update being commented on, with both IDs serving as foreign keys referencing the User and Update tables, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "A social networking platform manages its users' account information and the interactions among users. Users must provide a username when registering and may optionally provide an email address and phone number. Users can enter their date of birth and upload a personal avatar; the system stores the file path for the avatar. Each user account's creation time and the time of the last information modification are recorded.\n\nUsers can post updates on the platform, which may include text, images, or videos. Each update has a posting time and content type. Users can follow each other, with the follow relationship including the follower and the followed, and the follow time is recorded.\n\nAdditionally, users can comment on other users' updates. Comment details include the comment content, comment time, and commenter information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0110.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0110\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar_path` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` date DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`username`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `update` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `content_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `posted_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `update_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`username`) REFERENCES `user` (`username`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `follow_relationship` (\n  `follower_username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `followed_username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `followed_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`follower_username`, `followed_username`),\n  CONSTRAINT `follow_relationship_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`follower_username`) REFERENCES `user` (`username`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `follow_relationship_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`followed_username`) REFERENCES `user` (`username`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `comment` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `content` text NOT NULL,\n  `commented_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `update_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`username`) REFERENCES `user` (`username`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `comment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`update_id`) REFERENCES `update` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
